|money drop = 1,800¢ - 7,110¢
}}

==Enemy==
A stronger [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] that trades [[Immune to Slow|slow immunity]] for protection from [[Weaken|weaken]], and [[Savage Blow|Savage Blows]] for rare yet deadly [[Toxic]] hits that take 50% HP off of those afflicted. In the end, though, Casaurian Darkjo still isn't without his weaknesses, for he also has more than twice as many knockbacks as Ahirujo.

==Strategy==
Treat this enemy as you would Ahirujo. Due to his higher damage output, stronger meatshields as well as Dark-[[Resistant|resistant]] meatshields such as [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] or [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]] are needed. It is also important to note that [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] and his variants do not tank against Darkjo as effectively as against Ahirujo, though [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], with appropriate [[Talents]], has no such issue.

Rushers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] remain questionable against Darkjo, but [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] and Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] could be worthwhile thanks to their [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] to Darks. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is still very effective, even though his massive damage does not apply here, and a high-leveled [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] with his [[Wave Attack]] Talent unlocked might be worth using as well. Just remember that Darkjo's Toxic attacks can easily rend most units except for [[:Category:Cats with Toxic Immunity|those immune]].

